    @section xmlentityreferences Entity References

    References to internal parsed entities declared in a document's internal DTD subset are replaced by their
    replacement text, in element content and attribute values, including entities that reference other entities or
    contain markup (XML 1.0 section 4.4.3). Predefined and character references are unaffected.

    External entities are never loaded: a reference to an external general or parameter entity fails the parse
    with an error naming the entity's URI, instead of reading a local file or network resource (XXE) or silently
    dropping the reference. Entity expansion is bounded by libxml2's amplification limit, so a "billion laughs"
    document fails with an error. With a libxml2 older than 2.14, which cannot refuse external entities per parser,
    entity references are not expanded.

    @section xmlgenerationopts XML Generation Options

    Formatting and other serialization settings can be given as a hash to @ref Qore::Xml::make_xml() "make_xml()"
    and @ref Qore::Xml::XmlDoc::constructor() "XmlDoc::constructor()". Options that are not set keep their
    defaults, and unknown keys are ignored:

    |!Key|!Type|!Default|!Description
    |\c docVersion|\c string|\c "1.0"|the XML version of the generated document
    |\c encoding|\c string|\c "UTF-8"|the output character encoding
    |\c formatWithWhitespaces|\c bool|\c False|adds indentation and line breaks, like @ref Qore::Xml::XGF_ADD_FORMATTING
    |\c useNumericRefs|\c bool|\c False|writes non-ASCII characters as numeric character references, like \
        @ref Qore::Xml::XGF_USE_NUMERIC_REFS
    |\c dateFormat|\c string|\c "YYYYMMDDHHmmSS"|the format of serialized date/time values

    @code{.py}
hash<auto> opts = {
    "encoding": "ISO-8859-1",
    "formatWithWhitespaces": True,
};
string xml = make_xml({"order": {"id": 1}}, opts);
    @endcode
*/
